WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:05.407
We bought this old rusty pig trailer
 to turn&nbsp;it into a tiny house.

00:00:05.791 --> 00:00:07.033
What do you think about it?

00:00:07.609 --> 00:00:08.885
- It's rough.

00:00:08.885 --> 00:00:12.179
In the previous videos, you could see us 
stripping&nbsp;it and putting in the walls.

00:00:12.179 --> 00:00:15.221
In this video, we're going to make it waterproof.

00:00:15.221 --> 00:00:18.332
And,&nbsp;we're also going to continue 
clearing the road, that we started last week.

00:00:18.332 --> 00:00:21.205
Just so we can have&nbsp;an emergency exit in case of wildfires.

00:00:21.205 --> 00:00:23.362
Welcome to a new Project Kamp update.

00:00:23.938 --> 00:00:26.086
Okay, it's time to get&nbsp;started inside the trailer!

00:00:26.086 --> 00:00:28.939
However, we noticed it's not that easy to get into...

00:00:29.515 --> 00:00:31.926
Yeah, we could use&nbsp;a stairs before getting started.

00:00:33.511 --> 00:00:35.235
- So, that's why we need the ladder.

00:00:36.611 --> 00:00:41.748
Here, we have our beautiful&nbsp;ladder or stairs
 that we found at the scrapyard.

00:00:41.748 --> 00:00:49.628
Since it's needing of a bit of a&nbsp;touchup,
 we'll cut it at a right degree angle.

00:00:50.653 --> 00:00:55.115
And then, we'll most likely weld plates to it,
so we can secure that.

00:00:55.115 --> 00:00:57.301
It shouldn't be too much trouble.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:03.196
It's going to be a fun one!

00:01:03.964 --> 00:01:05.081
What are&nbsp;you doing up there?

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:07.613
- I'm setting up a GoPro for you!

00:01:07.613 --> 00:01:09.033
Thank you!

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:47.345
- I don't know if you know this Robert,
but it's&nbsp;a bit too high...

00:01:47.345 --> 00:01:48.935
A little bit!

00:01:48.935 --> 00:01:49.816
- But, it's okay.

00:01:49.816 --> 00:01:56.368
For now, we're going to just make 
two posts here with&nbsp;beams and another step.

00:01:56.800 --> 00:02:00.272
So, yeah, let's make that.

00:02:06.120 --> 00:02:08.521
- The ladder is in place and it&nbsp;feels sturdy.

00:02:08.521 --> 00:02:10.208
Let's go to the next step!

00:02:28.277 --> 00:02:30.810
Okay, so, we want to start putting the roof&nbsp;in.

00:02:31.645 --> 00:02:36.300
But, for that, we have to put this vapor barrier and install it.

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:40.047
Also, we have to finish&nbsp;the windows and the door.

00:02:40.047 --> 00:02:42.884
So, we are going to be doing 
two processes at the same time.

00:02:43.630 --> 00:02:45.367
Two&nbsp;people are going to be working on the roof.

00:02:45.367 --> 00:02:47.186
One is going to be finishing the windows.

00:02:47.186 --> 00:02:48.416
So, yeah...

00:02:48.416 --> 00:02:52.462
We&nbsp;start setting up the foil for the insulation,
 that we will add later.

00:02:52.462 --> 00:02:55.138
We are going to try out a new kind of material.

00:02:55.138 --> 00:02:58.224
Insulation made out of old textile and clothes.

00:02:58.224 --> 00:03:01.108
It seems like a nice way&nbsp;to reuse use those materials!

00:03:01.108 --> 00:03:06.424
But, the downside is that this material 
cannot get wet, or else&nbsp;it will get moldy...

00:03:06.968 --> 00:03:12.324
So, we need to add this new waterproof layer
 or vapor barrier, to make sure it&nbsp;stays dry.

00:03:12.324 --> 00:03:16.417
It feels nice to use recycled materials,
 but we don't like adding this new foil...

00:03:16.417 --> 00:03:18.859
Let us know&nbsp;what you think about it in the comments section.

00:03:18.859 --> 00:03:21.737
Anyway, for now, we're going to give this a try.

00:03:21.737 --> 00:03:24.964
Well, let's see if we can even manage with this wind...

00:03:26.357 --> 00:03:27.438
So, we're struggling a bit!

00:03:27.438 --> 00:03:34.568
The wind is&nbsp;just blowing the tarp into the trailer all the time!

00:03:34.568 --> 00:03:37.094
And, it's throwing our GoPro off.

00:03:37.094 --> 00:03:43.129
So, I&nbsp;think we're going to start folding
 and then we just finish this last part here.

00:03:43.129 --> 00:03:47.104
Because,&nbsp;it's just impossible with the wind...

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:18.216
Now that the foil is all rolled&nbsp;up,
Wouter can continue with the windows.

00:04:29.229 --> 00:04:31.494
- All right! The foil is in!

00:04:31.494 --> 00:04:35.713
We have little water&nbsp;repellent edge, so the water cannot run in.

00:04:36.973 --> 00:04:41.909
But, still, there was a bit of hole here, which would leak.

00:04:41.909 --> 00:04:45.710
So, I will patch it with some leftovers.

00:04:47.260 --> 00:04:53.454
I will put it behind the other foil,
 so when water runs from here, it will run off.

00:04:54.126 --> 00:04:57.767
Just so it doesn't creep in between this two layers.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:13.169
- We got this aluminium sheet, 
when we were stripping&nbsp;the trailer before.

00:05:13.169 --> 00:05:14.926
It was on the back of the door.

00:05:14.926 --> 00:05:17.337
It's a bit too hard to reuse this.

00:05:17.337 --> 00:05:19.165
It's&nbsp;all bended and bumpy...

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.585
We're going to use smaller parts
 to make the edges of the windows.

00:05:23.585 --> 00:05:26.601
This will make sure the rain water will flow out.

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:54.157
- So, this is the first rafter we're going to put&nbsp;in.

00:06:54.157 --> 00:06:58.358
We have the vapor barrier.

00:07:00.191 --> 00:07:02.366
We're going to&nbsp;start putting the rafters in.

00:07:02.366 --> 00:07:03.346
The first one.

00:07:35.600 --> 00:07:36.789
- So, what are we doing here?

00:07:36.789 --> 00:07:38.912
We're going to even out the beams.

00:07:38.912 --> 00:07:41.134
We just put all the rafters in.

00:07:42.284 --> 00:07:47.946
But, we didn't really measure it,
 if they are all sticking out the same amount.

00:07:47.946 --> 00:07:49.543
Or, the same size...

00:07:49.543 --> 00:07:55.955
So, right now, I'm going to&nbsp;mark this first beam 
at 10 centimeters, and then the last one there.

00:07:56.914 --> 00:07:58.089
I'll drive a nail in.

00:07:59.923 --> 00:08:03.949
We&nbsp;don't have a chalk line, but we can use rope.

00:08:03.949 --> 00:08:08.159
We'll put the rope and just mark all the beams at the&nbsp;same size.

00:08:08.159 --> 00:08:09.676
So, yeah...

00:08:09.676 --> 00:08:10.991
It's much faster.

00:08:10.991 --> 00:08:13.088
- Sounds good!

00:08:20.401 --> 00:08:21.583
Some video maker advice!

00:08:21.583 --> 00:08:24.659
Always keep an&nbsp;eye out that the microphone is NOT in the frame.

00:08:27.815 --> 00:08:30.339
- Right now, this line is straight.

00:08:30.339 --> 00:08:32.136
The beams are sticking out a bit.

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:38.010
So, we're going to mark them and cut them off.

00:08:42.095 --> 00:08:44.586
It took a while to cut all the tips of the&nbsp;rafters.

00:08:44.586 --> 00:08:46.347
But finally, they are in.

00:08:46.347 --> 00:08:51.435
As a next step, we will be putting wood boards
 on top, while also&nbsp;placing the windows

00:08:51.435 --> 00:08:54.349
But, for all that, we first needed to get materials.

00:08:58.338 --> 00:09:01.768
We want to make this trailer with 
as much secondhand materials as possible.

00:09:01.768 --> 00:09:05.097
But, it's quite hard&nbsp;to find old things around here...

00:09:05.097 --> 00:09:07.548
Especially if you look for sturdy decent things.

00:09:07.548 --> 00:09:10.663
There&nbsp;just aren't many people or companies doing this.

00:09:10.663 --> 00:09:14.347
So, it always takes quite some time&nbsp;to find some.

00:09:15.206 --> 00:09:19.389
But, we found a few places 
close by that might have something!

00:09:19.805 --> 00:09:21.319
So, let's&nbsp;have a look!

00:09:21.319 --> 00:09:23.580
First up: a place with wooden windows.

00:09:55.810 --> 00:09:59.418
We found the first one, but&nbsp;unfortunately,
 they didn't have much at this place...

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:05.581
So, let's try another place to find the rest.

00:10:10.685 --> 00:10:13.302
- Let's find some windows for the pig trailer.

00:10:14.970 --> 00:10:18.458
Most people in Portugal have aluminum
 frames in the windows.

00:10:19.728 --> 00:10:23.547
We&nbsp;found a place where they make windows,
 but they also replace windows.

00:10:23.547 --> 00:10:26.256
So, they have leftovers or secondhand windows.

00:10:26.256 --> 00:10:29.533
But, they also have here a 
stash of old wooden window windows.

00:10:29.533 --> 00:10:33.303
They just use it to burn it in the
 workspace to heat up during the winter.

00:10:34.498 --> 00:10:35.415
- They don't&nbsp;like wood?

00:10:35.415 --> 00:10:37.763
They don't like wood, like the old times.

00:10:51.352 --> 00:10:52.921
We found some windows here.

00:10:54.825 --> 00:10:56.010
Jackpot!

00:11:06.032 --> 00:11:07.453
These are our new windows, guys.

00:11:07.453 --> 00:11:10.359
We're going to get this, this and this.

00:11:11.983 --> 00:11:15.055
A fine glass insulation.

00:11:15.055 --> 00:11:17.217
Let's see what they look like!

00:11:17.217 --> 00:11:19.083
- We need to get some wood for the inside.

00:11:19.083 --> 00:11:21.288
So, we're back at the sawmill!

00:11:21.288 --> 00:11:25.970
Let's get some more of that basketball court.

00:11:27.514 --> 00:11:31.445
You might remember that we have already 
used these boards from an old basketball court.&nbsp;

00:11:31.445 --> 00:11:32.894
This was during the renovating of the yellow van.

00:11:33.566 --> 00:11:35.799
Luckily, they still have a big amount of it!

00:11:36.496 --> 00:11:40.295
It actually&nbsp;seems that no one around here 
really likes to work with it...

00:11:40.295 --> 00:11:43.831
Since, it's not the easiest&nbsp;to work with.

00:11:45.233 --> 00:11:46.783
It's so sketchy!

00:11:47.800 --> 00:11:51.814
The amount is still the same as before, so that's good for&nbsp;us.

00:11:51.814 --> 00:11:59.120
The only downside is that the good ones are at the bottom...

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:03.116
So, we are choosing all the boards.

00:12:03.116 --> 00:12:07.478
It's difficult&nbsp;to find boards that are without lines and stuff.

00:12:07.478 --> 00:12:09.627
So, we stopped being picky about that.

00:12:09.627 --> 00:12:13.426
But, we finally&nbsp;found out where the basketball court is from!

00:12:13.426 --> 00:12:15.705
It's from Tondela.

00:12:17.626 --> 00:12:22.521
Now that we have all the materials&nbsp;we need,
it's time to place the windows we just got.

00:14:07.160 --> 00:14:10.160
At the same time, we are also&nbsp;working on the basketball roof.

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:13.240
We're getting close to make the&nbsp;big trailer ready for some rain.

00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:11.730
Here we are on our beautiful roof!

00:15:11.730 --> 00:15:14.007
Yesterday&nbsp;was a really productive day!

00:15:14.007 --> 00:15:16.270
We finished quite a lot.

00:15:16.270 --> 00:15:20.341
We have just this last piece&nbsp;here to fill up.

00:15:20.341 --> 00:15:22.262
We're going to do that this morning.

00:15:22.262 --> 00:15:28.600
And then, we are going to cut&nbsp;off the edges
 and square up the roof.

00:15:42.240 --> 00:15:44.618
So, we didn't measure the length&nbsp;of the boards.

00:15:44.618 --> 00:15:47.721
Because, I can now cut everything off with the tracksaw.

00:15:47.721 --> 00:15:51.711
So, I'm going to measure 
and mark up where I have to cut.

00:15:51.711 --> 00:15:58.600
I'll cut everything&nbsp;off flush with this beam of the tracksaw.

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:30.000
I think that's enough.

00:16:39.968 --> 00:16:45.701
So, we're going to finish putting the vapor barrier on.

00:16:46.694 --> 00:16:50.710
We're going to put it on top
 and seal it with aluminum tape.

00:16:53.347 --> 00:16:58.480
As fast&nbsp;as possible too, because this thing gets hot fast!

00:17:31.880 --> 00:17:35.571
Okay, so, welcome to a closed pig trailer.

00:17:35.571 --> 00:17:38.454
Finally, the pig trail is almost waterproof.

00:17:38.454 --> 00:17:42.078
We installed three old aluminium windows and&nbsp;a big wooden one.

00:17:42.078 --> 00:17:46.403
They all have double glass and a little aluminium strip
 on the bottom to&nbsp;guide the water away.

00:17:46.403 --> 00:17:48.977
We also installed a big old wooden door.

00:17:48.977 --> 00:17:53.115
We've put the rafters on the roof&nbsp;that hold up 
the basketball court from the close by town.

00:17:53.659 --> 00:17:57.056
As you can see, it still has some stickers&nbsp;on it from gym.

00:17:57.689 --> 00:18:00.077
We also installed the stairs at the entrance.

00:18:00.077 --> 00:18:02.032
And, we have installed the foil on&nbsp;the walls.

00:18:02.704 --> 00:18:05.745
It's still rolled up as we have to put the insulation first.

00:18:05.745 --> 00:18:08.625
But, you will see that in&nbsp;the next updates.

00:18:08.625 --> 00:18:11.708
Subscribe and follow to see how we continue!

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:25.297
- All right, so, nice work on the pig trailer!

00:18:25.297 --> 00:18:26.885
We'll continue working on that.

00:18:26.885 --> 00:18:29.200
But, for now, we're going to finish up the road.

00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:30.559
We started this a few&nbsp;weeks ago.

00:18:30.559 --> 00:18:33.860
We have cleaned the left side of the road for a fire exit.

00:18:33.860 --> 00:18:37.248
So, in case everything burns&nbsp;down, we can safely go out.

00:18:37.248 --> 00:18:40.115
And now, we're going to continue cleaning the right side.

00:18:40.115 --> 00:18:41.501
It's very similar!

00:18:41.501 --> 00:18:44.149
It also has a lot of mimosas and a lot of spiky bushes.

00:18:44.149 --> 00:18:49.508
But, a big difference is that it also has a lot 
of&nbsp;native trees and a nice view from our big old ruin.

00:18:49.508 --> 00:18:51.293
So, it should give a good end result!

00:18:51.293 --> 00:18:53.163
But, it's&nbsp;going to be a lot of work...

00:18:53.163 --> 00:18:54.346
So, we're going to get some help.

00:18:55.032 --> 00:18:56.561
- Okay, it's still early in the morning.

00:18:56.561 --> 00:19:01.812
Some&nbsp;friends are going to come, because we have some friends
locally living that really are willing&nbsp;to help.

00:19:01.812 --> 00:19:06.527
So, we invited them for today,
 and we will take on the second half of the road.

00:19:06.527 --> 00:19:10.766
First, a hot&nbsp;drink while gathering together,
 and then we're going to start!

00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:23.408
Okay, today is the day that we're going
 to&nbsp;take down these big mimosas.

00:20:24.305 --> 00:20:28.335
Because, in the back, there are many nature of trees
 that we want&nbsp;to give priority to.

00:20:29.174 --> 00:20:31.638
So, these ones are going to go down.

00:20:34.737 --> 00:20:58.120
- Morning!

00:22:30.440 --> 00:22:31.799
We now have a different approach!

00:22:31.799 --> 00:22:36.283
Because, we can't&nbsp;cut the trees so they will fall over this road.

00:22:36.283 --> 00:22:38.596
They will always fall back.

00:22:38.596 --> 00:22:39.812
So, that's what we're&nbsp;going to do.

00:22:39.812 --> 00:22:43.835
We're going to cut the trees,
and make them smaller when they're down.

00:22:44.603 --> 00:22:48.040
I'm going to&nbsp;clear this first and then we can work.

00:23:00.680 --> 00:23:04.493
As you can see, the job went well!

00:23:04.493 --> 00:23:07.910
All of the&nbsp;oaks are nice, healthy and intact!

00:23:07.910 --> 00:23:09.837
So, it works nice.

00:23:09.837 --> 00:23:16.449
It could have be worse, but at the end,
you can see the end result of those two.

00:23:34.600 --> 00:23:35.804
- What's happening Ale?

00:23:36.604 --> 00:23:42.799
I have brambles, sawdust&nbsp;and Mimosas all over the place, so...

00:23:44.026 --> 00:23:48.324
Every once in a while you have to clean
 a&nbsp;bit, because it's too much.

00:23:48.804 --> 00:23:52.598
- Some mimosas are very big like this one,
 which just got cut down.

00:23:52.598 --> 00:23:57.784
This one&nbsp;is going to Hans to be used as firewood, I think.

00:24:39.640 --> 00:24:41.734
- So, another day, another job done!

00:24:41.734 --> 00:24:44.058
You can see that no&nbsp;mimosas are around!

00:24:44.058 --> 00:24:45.926
Now, we have a nice and clear space.

00:24:49.436 --> 00:24:52.981
- The rest of the area&nbsp;to clear was mainly a brush cutting job.

00:24:52.981 --> 00:24:57.760
It's nothing too special,&nbsp;but it's somehow satisfying to watch!

00:26:37.600 --> 00:26:42.453
- Okay guys, so, we recently finished the right side of the&nbsp;road.

00:26:42.453 --> 00:26:44.485
Let me show you the results now!

00:26:44.485 --> 00:26:48.834
So, where I'm walking right now, you couldn't make a move.

00:26:48.834 --> 00:26:49.604
You&nbsp;couldn't get here!

00:26:49.604 --> 00:26:51.538
This was all fully overgrown!

00:26:51.538 --> 00:26:54.173
Brambles, ferns and multiple kinds of bushes.

00:26:54.813 --> 00:26:58.193
But, as you&nbsp;can see, the space is fully open now.

00:26:59.186 --> 00:27:04.216
Only the natives remain, which is very cool&nbsp;for them to thrive!

00:27:04.216 --> 00:27:08.530
We found or rediscovered these fruit trees.

00:27:08.530 --> 00:27:11.549
We planted these last&nbsp;years,
 but they didn't have any space to grow...

00:27:11.549 --> 00:27:14.373
Now, they are free and happy.

00:27:14.373 --> 00:27:21.136
So, down&nbsp;here after this slope,
 we did loads and loads of brush cutting here!

00:27:21.136 --> 00:27:25.082
And now, it's just clean,&nbsp;neat and nice.

00:27:25.082 --> 00:27:27.453
This area we also brush cutted a lot!

00:27:27.453 --> 00:27:31.494
We had to do some manual work
 to free up&nbsp;the natives as well.

00:27:33.068 --> 00:27:37.000
Right now, we have the neighbors biological brush cutters.

00:27:37.000 --> 00:27:40.732
All right,&nbsp;so, we tackled clearing the sides of the roads.

00:27:40.732 --> 00:27:46.463
We had a lot of mimosas, brambles 
and bushes&nbsp;to defeat, but we won!

00:27:46.463 --> 00:27:48.983
And, now that the job is done...

00:27:48.983 --> 00:27:51.688
As you can see, it's beautiful.

00:27:51.688 --> 00:27:57.520
So, we can&nbsp;enjoy the scenery, while going back to Basekamp.

00:28:02.520 --> 00:28:04.238
- The road is now cleaned up

00:28:04.238 --> 00:28:06.059
It's now much safer in case&nbsp;of a fire.

00:28:06.059 --> 00:28:10.802
We also freed up the native trees,
 so they can grow into big trees now, which is cool.

00:28:10.802 --> 00:28:13.931
And, in general, the whole land here is now much easier to maintain!

00:28:13.931 --> 00:28:17.343
Because, we can just keep&nbsp;it low 
with a brush cutter, so it doesn't get wild again.

00:28:18.260 --> 00:28:21.874
Now, we got a lot of mimosas,
 and&nbsp;we're going to give the office a little upgrade!

00:28:21.874 --> 00:28:25.347
It's involving one of the favorite&nbsp;things of you guys: Kevin!

00:28:25.347 --> 00:28:30.387
We're going to use the mimosas, some old jeans
 and a sewing machine&nbsp;to make something useful.

00:28:30.387 --> 00:28:32.633
It's been a hot summer in Kamp.

00:28:32.633 --> 00:28:36.268
The windows let the sun get&nbsp;in
 and it heats up the whole office!

00:28:36.652 --> 00:28:40.380
We tried putting cork on the windows 
and the principle&nbsp;works, but...

00:28:40.380 --> 00:28:42.493
This setup feels too improvised.

00:28:42.493 --> 00:28:44.383
So, we thought: ''Let's make some curtains.''

00:28:44.799 --> 00:28:47.319
We're&nbsp;going to use some of the mimosas that we cut before.

00:28:53.784 --> 00:28:57.560
The first stem will be used&nbsp;as a bar,
 so we make sure it's smooth.

00:29:17.880 --> 00:29:21.960
With the second trunk,
 we will&nbsp;create the support for the main bar.

00:29:57.040 --> 00:30:01.895
- So, we have this jeans material 
left&nbsp;over from the previous project.

00:30:01.895 --> 00:30:05.097
And, we are going to make a curtain out of it for the office.

00:31:30.560 --> 00:31:32.022
It's done!

00:31:44.914 --> 00:31:46.992
- So, now we have some nice thick curtains.

00:31:46.992 --> 00:31:49.916
They really keep the sun outside,
so it prevents the building from heating up.

00:31:49.916 --> 00:31:53.154
Which is good, because&nbsp;makes it a bit 
more comfortable to work here.

00:31:56.356 --> 00:31:58.584
All right, so, that was it for this video!

00:31:58.584 --> 00:32:01.626
In the next video, we're going to continue working on the pig trailer.

00:32:01.626 --> 00:32:03.600
And, we're going to&nbsp;build something special!

00:32:04.048 --> 00:32:06.762
